{
  "protocol": {
    "scope": "Development at four PINNS locations already examined. Each outer fold holds out one complete physical site; its labels and features never enter any model, feature scaling or threshold selection for that fold. Thresholds are specific to the outer training sites, event and feature family. No independent new-site validation.",
    "events": "Over the next 30 samples (3 s), apply the archived coordinate-derived start and stop definitions. Five historical samples span 0.4 s. Start eligibility requires mean pre-event speed <=0.20 m/s, stop >=0.60 m/s, using only the last three causal smoothed historical speeds. Scores are 0 and decisions negative outside the event's eligibility mask, including at threshold 0.",
    "methods": "All-eligible dummy scores one for an eligible row. Three feature families are fixed from the published five-frame probe: motion, motion plus the last normalized pose, and both plus four ordered masked joint changes. Fit each event separately, on eligible rows only. Equal window weights, no resampling or class weights. Training-only population mean and SD, divisor 1 for constant features. Fixed C=0.1; summed logistic loss + squared coefficient norm/(2C), unpenalized intercept. An eligible training set containing one class predicts its observed frequency; an empty eligible training set predicts zero.",
    "threshold": "Within the three outer training sites, hold out each site in turn and fit on the other two. Pool the three inner OOF scores over eligible training windows. Among distinct observed OOF scores choose the highest threshold maximizing pooled eligible F1; prediction is score >= threshold. No eligible inner rows or no inner positives: use fixed 0.5. Refit on all three outer training sites, then evaluate once on the fourth. Compare to fixed 0.5 on the identical outer probabilities.",
    "metrics": "TP, FP and FN use all outer windows and the eligibility decision gate. AP is non-interpolated, grouped at score ties, and uses scores independently of threshold. Also report AP within history-eligible rows. If the evaluation group has no positives, AP/F1 are null and all confusion counts remain. Four-site macro averages AP/F1 equally over sites with actual positives for that event, giving the denominator; confusion counts are also averaged over all four sites and pooled sums are provided. OOF fits share development locations and observations within a clip may be correlated."
  },
